@@ -5,3 +5,27 @@ All webhook routes answer within a few milliseconds: they store the event and qu
 ## Carrier
 
 `POST /hooks/carrier`. The carrier sends the shared `CARRIER_TOKEN` in `X-Carrier-Token`. It retries a delivery until it gets a 2xx answer.
+
+## Payments
+
+`POST /hooks/payments`. Set `PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_SECRET` to the signing secret that the dashboard of the provider shows.
+
+Each delivery has this header:
+
+```
+X-Payments-Signature: t=1700000000,v1=5f2b...e1
+```
+
+- `t` is the signing time as Unix seconds.
+- `v1` is the lowercase hex HMAC-SHA256 of `<t>.<raw body>` with the signing secret. During a secret rotation, the header has two `v1` values; either one is enough.
+
+The route answers:
+
+| Status | When |
+|---|---|
+| 202 | A new event of a handled type. The job is queued. |
+| 200 | A duplicate delivery, or an event type that the job does not handle. The provider stops retrying. |
+| 400 | No valid signature header, a signing time more than 5 minutes off, or a body that is not JSON. |
+| 401 | No `v1` value matches. |
+
+The provider retries each delivery with a backoff for 3 days until it gets a 2xx answer, and it can send one event more than once. The event ID makes each event count once.
